{"content_hash": "646610a79ad5634a", "version_id": 1044, "article_id": 105, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Meta controls 85% of AI glasses while China's market splits", "title_zh": "Meta拿下全球八成AI眼镜，中国市场还在各自混战", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "tmtpost", "source_url": "https://www.tmtpost.com/8213674.html", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689439518196-f48a24b49fb5?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OHx8bWV0YXxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzk1MzExMDg5fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Julio Lopez on Unsplash", "author": "Julio Lopez", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@juliolopez?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-person-holding-up-a-cell-phone-in-front-of-a-sign-ilbjfRwOgzA?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(186, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(224, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "8382d9bae0e2"}}, "published_date": "2026-11-22", "word_count": 263, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Meta now sells more than eight out of ten AI glasses worldwide, but no single Chinese company comes close at home. New products keep arriving, yet sales in China have started to fall.", "lead_zh": "全球每卖出十副AI眼镜，就有八副来自Meta，但在中国本土，没有一家公司能接近这个位置。新品不断上市，可中国市场的销量却开始下滑。", "preview": "During this year's Double 11 shopping festival, several Chinese brands claimed first place in different categories. Thunderbird Innovation s", "preview_zh": "今年双11，多个中国品牌在不同榜单上宣称第一。雷鸟创新称登顶京东智能眼镜与XR设备榜，阿里夸克称S1型号领跑XR热卖榜。但中国整体市场没有一家公司占据明显优势。Omdia数据显示，2026年上半年，阿里、影目和小米的市场份额分别为17.4%、14.6%和14.0%。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 1027, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/105/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 116.75, "size_bytes": 701424, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 309, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/105/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 118.825, "size_bytes": 713952, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 309, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/105/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/105/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 126.525, "size_bytes": 760176, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 309, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/105/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/105/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 110.975, "size_bytes": 666864, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 309, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/105/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/105/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 119.9, "size_bytes": 720288, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 309, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/105/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@62070c4b/content/data/versions/1044.json", "paragraphs": ["During this year's Double 11 shopping festival, several Chinese brands claimed first place in different categories. Thunderbird Innovation said it topped JD.com's smart glasses and XR rankings, while Alibaba's Quark said its S1 model led the XR sales chart. Yet no Chinese company holds a clear lead overall. In the first half of 2026, Alibaba, INMO and Xiaomi held 17.4%, 14.6% and 14.0% of the market, according to Omdia.", "The global picture is far more concentrated. Omdia says 8.7 million AI glasses were shipped in 2025, and Meta took 85.2% of them. Meta's early Ray-Ban Stories failed because of weak batteries, but the 2023 Ray-Ban Meta fixed those problems and added an AI assistant. Its partner EssilorLuxottica brought famous brands, lens factories and retail stores, so buyers could try glasses on like normal eyewear.", "Chinese companies are still testing different ideas. Xiaomi follows Meta's screen-free approach, Alibaba wants glasses to become an entry point for its services, and specialists such as Rokid and Thunderbird focus on displays. China now makes 45% of the world's AR and AI glasses with screens, Counterpoint reports, but it is unclear which design will win over ordinary buyers.", "Growth at home is slowing. IDC data shows Chinese smart glasses shipments fell 8% in the second quarter of 2026, the first drop on record, while screen-free models declined sharply. Thunderbird's CEO said more than 200 AI features launched in 2025, yet fewer than 6% are used long term. Return rates in some online channels reach 30%, and even 70% for a few products.", "Money separates Meta from Chinese startups."], "paragraphs_zh": ["今年双11，多个中国品牌在不同榜单上宣称第一。雷鸟创新称登顶京东智能眼镜与XR设备榜，阿里夸克称S1型号领跑XR热卖榜。但中国整体市场没有一家公司占据明显优势。Omdia数据显示，2026年上半年，阿里、影目和小米的市场份额分别为17.4%、14.6%和14.0%。", "全球格局则集中得多。Omdia称2025年全球AI眼镜出货870万副，Meta独占85.2%。Meta早期的Ray-Ban Stories因续航差而失败，但2023年的Ray-Ban Meta解决了这些问题并加入AI助手。合作伙伴依视路陆逊梯卡带来知名品牌、镜片工厂和零售门店，消费者能像买普通眼镜一样试戴。", "中国企业仍在尝试不同路线。小米走Meta式的无屏路线，阿里希望眼镜成为其服务的入口，Rokid和雷鸟等专业厂商则专注显示技术。Counterpoint称，中国占全球带屏AR与AI眼镜出货量的45%，但哪种设计能赢得普通消费者仍无定论。", "国内增长正在放缓。IDC数据显示，2026年第二季度中国智能眼镜出货量下降8%，为首次下滑，无屏机型跌得更狠。雷鸟CEO称2025年行业上线200多项AI功能，但长期使用率不到6%。部分线上渠道退货率达30%，个别产品甚至高达70%。", "资金把Meta和中国创业公司区分开来。Meta靠广告业务为Reality Labs输血，而XREAL在2025年毛利率改善的情况下仍净亏损4.56亿元。华为、阿里等大厂带来手机用户和服务，Rokid等小公司则接入微信支付和谷歌。Rokid创始人说，他关注日活和复购，而不是销量排名。"], "body": "During this year's Double 11 shopping festival, several Chinese brands claimed first place in different categories. Thunderbird Innovation said it topped JD.com's smart glasses and XR rankings, while Alibaba's Quark said its S1 model led the XR sales chart. Yet no Chinese company holds a clear lead overall. In the first half of 2026, Alibaba, INMO and Xiaomi held 17.4%, 14.6% and 14.0% of the market, according to Omdia.\n\nThe global picture is far more concentrated. Omdia says 8.7 million AI glasses were shipped in 2025, and Meta took 85.2% of them. Meta's early Ray-Ban Stories failed because of weak batteries, but the 2023 Ray-Ban Meta fixed those problems and added an AI assistant. Its partner EssilorLuxottica brought famous brands, lens factories and retail stores, so buyers could try glasses on like normal eyewear.\n\nChinese companies are still testing different ideas. Xiaomi follows Meta's screen-free approach, Alibaba wants glasses to become an entry point for its services, and specialists such as Rokid and Thunderbird focus on displays. China now makes 45% of the world's AR and AI glasses with screens, Counterpoint reports, but it is unclear which design will win over ordinary buyers.\n\nGrowth at home is slowing. IDC data shows Chinese smart glasses shipments fell 8% in the second quarter of 2026, the first drop on record, while screen-free models declined sharply. Thunderbird's CEO said more than 200 AI features launched in 2025, yet fewer than 6% are used long term. Return rates in some online channels reach 30%, and even 70% for a few products.\n\nMoney separates Meta from Chinese startups.", "body_zh": "今年双11，多个中国品牌在不同榜单上宣称第一。雷鸟创新称登顶京东智能眼镜与XR设备榜，阿里夸克称S1型号领跑XR热卖榜。但中国整体市场没有一家公司占据明显优势。Omdia数据显示，2026年上半年，阿里、影目和小米的市场份额分别为17.4%、14.6%和14.0%。\n\n全球格局则集中得多。Omdia称2025年全球AI眼镜出货870万副，Meta独占85.2%。Meta早期的Ray-Ban Stories因续航差而失败，但2023年的Ray-Ban Meta解决了这些问题并加入AI助手。合作伙伴依视路陆逊梯卡带来知名品牌、镜片工厂和零售门店，消费者能像买普通眼镜一样试戴。\n\n中国企业仍在尝试不同路线。小米走Meta式的无屏路线，阿里希望眼镜成为其服务的入口，Rokid和雷鸟等专业厂商则专注显示技术。Counterpoint称，中国占全球带屏AR与AI眼镜出货量的45%，但哪种设计能赢得普通消费者仍无定论。\n\n国内增长正在放缓。IDC数据显示，2026年第二季度中国智能眼镜出货量下降8%，为首次下滑，无屏机型跌得更狠。雷鸟CEO称2025年行业上线200多项AI功能，但长期使用率不到6%。部分线上渠道退货率达30%，个别产品甚至高达70%。\n\n资金把Meta和中国创业公司区分开来。Meta靠广告业务为Reality Labs输血，而XREAL在2025年毛利率改善的情况下仍净亏损4.56亿元。华为、阿里等大厂带来手机用户和服务，Rokid等小公司则接入微信支付和谷歌。Rokid创始人说，他关注日活和复购，而不是销量排名。", "text": "During this year's Double 11 shopping festival, several Chinese brands claimed first place in different categories. Thunderbird Innovation said it topped JD.com's smart glasses and XR rankings, while Alibaba's Quark said its S1 model led the XR sales chart. Yet no Chinese company holds a clear lead overall. In the first half of 2026, Alibaba, INMO and Xiaomi held 17.4%, 14.6% and 14.0% of the market, according to Omdia. The global picture is far more concentrated. Omdia says 8.7 million AI glasses were shipped in 2025, and Meta took 85.2% of them. Meta's early Ray-Ban Stories failed because of weak batteries, but the 2023 Ray-Ban Meta fixed those problems and added an AI assistant. Its partner EssilorLuxottica brought famous brands, lens factories and retail stores, so buyers could try glasses on like normal eyewear. Chinese companies are still testing different ideas. Xiaomi follows Meta's screen-free approach, Alibaba wants glasses to become an entry point for its services, and specialists such as Rokid and Thunderbird focus on displays. China now makes 45% of the world's AR and AI glasses with screens, Counterpoint reports, but it is unclear which design will win over ordinary buyers. Growth at home is slowing. IDC data shows Chinese smart glasses shipments fell 8% in the second quarter of 2026, the first drop on record, while screen-free models declined sharply. Thunderbird's CEO said more than 200 AI features launched in 2025, yet fewer than 6% are used long term. Return rates in some online channels reach 30%, and even 70% for a few products. Money separates Meta from Chinese startups.", "vocab": [{"word": "concentrated", "pos": "adj", "zh": "集中的", "note": "形容市场由少数公司主导", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "shipment", "pos": "noun", "zh": "出货量", "note": "常用复数 shipments", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "market share", "pos": "phra